## Data and third-party content

The AGPL above covers the source code in this repository. The data files carry
the terms of where the data came from.

**scripts/charts.json** — Billboard Year-End Hot 100 rankings from 1980 on,
parsed from the English Wikipedia article for each year
(<https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Billboard_Year-End_Hot_100_singles_of_the_year>).
Wikipedia text is licensed CC BY-SA 4.0
(<https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/>). This derived data is
distributed under CC BY-SA 4.0, not the AGPL; keep this attribution and the same
licence if you redistribute it.

**src/data/songs.json, src/data/schedule.json, src/data/schedule-world.json,
scripts/misses.json, scripts/first-years.json** — song titles, artist names,
years and genres are factual metadata. Track ids, preview URLs and artwork URLs
point at Apple's iTunes preview service. The recordings and cover art belong to
the respective rights holders and to Apple; this repository grants no licence to
them and does not redistribute them — the browser streams previews from Apple's
servers at play time. If you deploy this project, review Apple's terms for the
iTunes Search API and for iTunes preview content first.

**scripts/world-cache.json** is a local scrape cache. It is not part of this
repository (see .gitignore) and is rebuilt by `npm run songs:world`.

**Song and artist names** are used for identification only.

